A||N||2||fieroshop||Oem or Ultimate dogbone||||1||
Z||000000||fieroshop||11-22-2000||11:00 AM||||Questions that I see all the time and ask of us here at the shop. My recommnedation is get an oem strut in place of the ultimate dogbone. I know that I will get a lot of people argue with me but I will explain.<BR>Having to replace several of the mounts that hold the dogbone and is bolted to the engine, These brackets go bad after a while due to the fact that there is no give in the poly bone and the holes get elongated and as you start of from a stop you hear a clunk, clunk that makes you think that there is something wrong with your motor mounts. These brckets are not meant to have a dogbone that has no give and wear out by the ultimate dogbone. <P><BR>------------------<BR> <BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroshop_sig_1.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by fieroshop (edited 11-23-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||11-22-2000||11:58 AM||||Exactly.||||reg||14
Z||000002||theogre||11-22-2000||01:49 PM||||Didn't we cover this already?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>I just generally think the polly strut is too hard. I don't like it in my 4 cyl setup but there's really no other choice unless someone has an extra set of automatic tranny brackets/mounts I can have. (I hate this monomount GM put in there. what a POS.)<P>OEM struts just cannot take the loads the monomount automatics give it. You'll trash the intake and/or exhaust parts with OE struts. A bracket is cheaper than a new TBI and intake. (more info about this in my cave.) You learn real quick to shove it in neutral at long trafic lights. Thing will rattle your teeth loose.<P>Other than the cradel mounts, and maybe the sway bar, I don't want any polly. My personal feeling is the stuff is way over rated for allot of things.||||reg||1
